1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,100
In nineteen sixty-six, someone stole the World Cup. A dog found it.

2
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,620
It's London, and England is hosting the World Cup in four months.

3
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:13,740
And the golden trophy is sitting in a glass case, at a— yeah, at a stamp show.

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:18,060
Then, on Sunday the twentieth of March, somebody takes it from the display.

5
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,480
Now the most famous trophy in sport is just gone.

6
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,960
Hit like if you'd have guarded it better than that.

7
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:29,140
But then a ransom note shows up. Ransom means pay us, or you never see it again.

8
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:33,700
It actually comes with a piece of the trophy's lining, from a man calling himself Jackson.

9
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,540
Then police arrest a London dockworker named Edward Betchley.

10
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:41,220
But Betchley says he's only the middleman, and that someone else stole it.

11
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,040
Who? He never tells them.

12
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,500
Send this to the friend who'd never snitch either.

13
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:49,360
So now the police have a note, a middleman, and still no trophy.

14
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:53,800
Then, one week after the theft, David Corbett walks his dog in south London.

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:58,260
Now his dog, Pickles, sniffs out a package under a hedge, wrapped in newspaper.

16
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,920
And inside? The World Cup trophy.

17
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:05,240
Wait, it gets better. Now the police briefly treat Corbett as a suspect.

18
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,760
Follow if you'd trust Pickles over the police.

19
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:11,960
Betchley is convicted over the ransom demand, and he's sentenced to two years.

20
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:15,800
And the actual thief? Nobody was ever convicted of stealing it.

21
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:19,940
And yeah, that summer England won the World Cup, and the hero was a dog.

22
00:01:20,420 --> 00:01:22,800
Police or Pickles, who really found the World Cup?

